---
/** Privacy Policy. DRAFT pending legal review. Static. */
import Legal from '../../layouts/Legal.astro';
import {staticContext} from '../../server/page';

export const prerender = true;

const {site, viewer} = await staticContext(Astro.request);
---

<Legal
  site={site}
  viewer={viewer}
  title="Privacy Policy"
  path="/legal/privacy"
  description="How NAMASTE International Inc., operating Conflict Intelligence Training, collects, uses and protects personal information under Canadian privacy law.">
  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      NAMASTE International Inc. (Canada) operates Conflict Intelligence Training: this website, our online community,
      our programs and our products. We are responsible for the personal information we collect and hold. Our privacy
      contact can be reached at <a href="mailto:hello@namasteintl.com">hello@namasteintl.com</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Name and email address</strong>, when you join the community, make a purchase or write to us.</li>
      <li><strong>Profile information</strong> you choose to add to your community profile.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Content members share</strong> in the community, such as posts, comments, messages and files.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Order information</strong>, such as what was purchased and the billing and shipping details needed to
        complete an order. Payment card details are entered with Stripe; we do not receive or store full card numbers.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Usage data</strong>, such as pages visited, the type of device and browser, IP address and how the
        community is used.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>Members may read in the community without posting. Sharing is always a choice.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To create and run your community account.</li>
      <li>To deliver our programs, the Conflict Exploration Kit and the Practitioner Certification.</li>
      <li>To process payments and ship orders.</li>
      <li>To send the emails you have asked for, and other updates where you have agreed to receive them.</li>
      <li>To reply when you write to us.</li>
      <li>To keep the community safe and to uphold the Community Guidelines.</li>
      <li>To understand how the website and community are used, so that we can improve them.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We collect and use personal information with your consent, and only for the purposes we describe here.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>Who processes it for us</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Our community platform</strong> (EzyCommunity) hosts this website and our community, including accounts,
        profiles and the content members share.
      </li>
      <li><strong>Stripe</strong> processes payments.</li>
      <li><strong>Encharge</strong> sends our emails.</li>
      <li><strong>Shipping carriers</strong> receive the name and address needed to deliver an order.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Google Fonts</strong> delivers the typeface this website uses, and receives your device's IP address when
        a page loads.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      These providers may store or process information outside Canada, including in the United States. When they do, the
      information is subject to the laws of the country where it is held.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      The community uses cookies to keep you signed in and to protect your account. These cookies are necessary: without
      them, signing in does not work. The website may also keep small settings in your browser, such as whether you have
      just signed in.
    </p>
    <p>
      Analytics or marketing cookies: <mark>[ANALYTICS AND MARKETING COOKIES: Ian to confirm whether any are used, and
      which]</mark>. Email open and click tracking: <mark>[EMAIL TRACKING: Ian to confirm whether it is enabled in
      Encharge]</mark>.
    </p>
    <p>You might choose to block or delete cookies in your browser settings, though signing in will then not work.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
      We keep personal information only as long as we need it for the purposes above, and then delete it or make it
      anonymous.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Account and profile information: <mark>[DATA RETENTION PERIOD FOR ACCOUNTS: Ian to confirm]</mark>.</li>
      <li>Order and payment records: <mark>[DATA RETENTION PERIOD FOR ORDER RECORDS: Ian to confirm]</mark>.</li>
      <li>Messages sent to us: <mark>[DATA RETENTION PERIOD FOR MESSAGES: Ian to confirm]</mark>.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>Access, correction, deletion and consent</h2>
    <p>You may ask us at any time to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>tell you what personal information we hold about you, and give you a copy;</li>
      <li>correct information that is inaccurate or incomplete;</li>
      <li>delete your information and close your account;</li>
      <li>withdraw your consent to a use of your information, including marketing emails.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Write to <a href="mailto:hello@namasteintl.com">hello@namasteintl.com</a>. We may ask you to confirm your identity
      first, and we reply within 30 days. Every marketing email also includes a link to unsubscribe. Withdrawing consent
      may mean we can no longer provide some services, and we will explain what that means when you ask.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>Keeping it safe</h2>
    <p>
      We use reasonable safeguards to protect personal information from loss, theft and unauthorized access. No system
      is perfectly secure, so we also ask members to share thoughtfully.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>Canadian privacy law</h2>
    <p>
      We handle personal information in line with Canada's Personal Information Protection and Electronic Documents Act
      (PIPEDA) and any provincial privacy law that applies. If you have a concern, we invite you to write to us first. You
      may also contact the Office of the Privacy Commissioner of Canada.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      When we change this policy, we update the effective date above. When a change is significant, we tell members by
      email or in the community.
    </p>
  </section>
</Legal>
